How To Build CustomOS and the CustomOS bootloader (Windows)

1. Download all of the files
2. Make a folder somewhere to store all of the files
3. Place the Compile.cmd script in the root of that folder.
4. Make a folder called "files" in the root of that folder.
5. Place all of the .h and .c files into the "files" folder.
Note: Make sure mingw-w64 is installed to the system PATH! (Windows)
6. Run the script
7. Find a way to run the bootx64.efi file. 
   I recommend installing QEMU and running the "Run QEMU.cmd" file also included, because it works perfectly.

8. Launch the VM (preferably by using the Run QEMU.cmd file listed above), and it should be self-explanatory from there.
